    <h4>Ejemplo: kube-bench</h4>
    <pre><code># Ejecutar CIS Benchmark
kubectl apply -f https://raw.githubusercontent.com/aquasecurity/kube-bench/main/job.yaml

# Ver resultados
kubectl logs job/kube-bench

# Ejecutar localmente
kube-bench run --targets master,node</code></pre>

    <h4>Ejemplo: Falco</h4>
    <pre><code># Instalar Falco
helm repo add falcosecurity https://falcosecurity.github.io/charts
helm install falco falcosecurity/falco

# Regla personalizada - detectar shell en contenedor
- rule: Shell in Container
  desc: Detect shell execution in container
  condition: >
    spawned_process and container and
    proc.name in (bash, sh, zsh)
  output: >
    Shell spawned in container
    (user=%user.name container=%container.name image=%container.image.repository)
  priority: WARNING</code></pre>

    <h3>15.4 Supply Chain Security</h3>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>Image signing:</strong> Cosign, Notary para firmar y verificar imágenes</li>
        <li><strong>SBOM (Software Bill of Materials):</strong> inventario de componentes</li>
        <li><strong>Admission webhooks:</strong> validar firmas antes de desplegar</li>
        <li><strong>Private registries:</strong> Harbor, ECR, ACR con scanning integrado</li>
    </ul>

    <h5>Ejemplo: Cosign</h5>
    <pre><code># Generar par de claves
cosign generate-key-pair

# Firmar imagen
cosign sign --key cosign.key myregistry.io/myapp:v1.0

# Verificar firma
cosign verify --key cosign.pub myregistry.io/myapp:v1.0</code></pre>

